// Nations: curated states and relationships (window.WORLD_POWERS). Edit by hand, then raise version and asOf.
// Dates are YYYY, YYYY-MM or YYYY-MM-DD. A node or edge with no "to" is still in effect.
// Nodes: measure is GDP in current US$ billions for its year, cited in refs; it is the node size and measures economic
//   size, not power. There are no influence or strength scores. entity picks a shared colour token (vocab.entities),
//   region follows UN M49 sub-regions (the EU spans several and has none), memberships name keys of vocab.memberships.
// Edges: type is the layer (security, hostility, economic, diplomatic) and kind names the sub-type. state is a short dated
//   description, asOf is when it was checked, reviewBy is when to check again. directed: true marks a tie that reads
//   source verb target (sanctions, coercion, dependency, accession). Review windows: 30 days for war, sanctions, talks
//   and truces; 90 days for trade, tariffs and fast-moving disputes; 12 months for treaties and memberships.
// grade: documented means a primary record or dataset is cited; reported means reliable secondary reporting only.
//   Nothing below that ships. Events from 2026 appear only with two independent sources, or are graded reported
//   with the outlet named in desc.
// refs name entries of sources. Sources of kind primary or dataset are official records; secondary is news or analysis.
// vocab.relations.*.kindMarks names the shape drawn in the middle of ties of each kind ("none" is a plain line);
//   vocab.memberships.*.total is the size of the whole group, so a chip reads "6 of 32".
